      "content": "idk, it feels like most ppl just dismiss it as \"racism\" without actually looking at the data. like, if you look at things like the Flynn effect or certain studies on heritability, doesn't that make the argument a bit more scientifically grounded than just being hateful? what kind of actual data or studies do they usually point to when they talk about these genetic differences?",
